of the unit’s one value, made afresh","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for each iteration.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The unit’s work runs in the signal’s task each time iteration begins; a unit that fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends the batched sequence with its error. When the batched sequence ends first, the unit’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work is cancelled; a unit whose work ignores cancellation keeps the batch’s internal task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alive until it returns, though the batched sequence itself ends at once. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject"},{"text":" takes ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CountBatchStrategy\/signal(_:)-2ind0"},{"text":" instead, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves the subject alone. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy runs the unit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anew and fires once when it completes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Example","anchor":"Example","level":2},{"code":["let reachable = DeferredTask { try await server.waitUntilReachable() }","for try await requests in outbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(20), .signal(reachable))) {","    try await send(requests)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"signal(_:)","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false},{"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"